e  wait what Final Fantasy 15 embraces  contemporary open-world principles from  the start outside of a few linear story  missions you're free to explore  sprawling environments and take on  dozens of side quests at your leisure  but dedicating your time to rewarding  pursuits has a side effect the more  comfortable you become living in AOS  doing honest work the further away and  less important noctis's concerns feel it  doesn't help that most NPCs would rather  talk about their magazine publishing  business or recipes than important world  affairs and as far as your bodyguards  are concerned their content cruising  around AOS and their fancy car cracking  jokes and taking selfies with noctis's  crew gladiolus the muscle Ignace the  brains and Prompto the comic relief what  you see is what you get each character  is treated to a time in the spotlight  during story missions but these events  which seem major in the moment have  little long-term impact they make for  upbeat travel companions offering tons  of colourful banter during your travels  but it is disappointing to see  supporting characters a group that  typically has diverse backgrounds and  curious personalities in Final Fantasy  games relegated to cliched unbending  roles  she's a messenger a spirit faithful to  the Oracle Oh for real during the first  half of the story missions are designed  to familiarize you with the ebb and flow  of the open world but more importantly  you learn how to fight there's a lot to  manage despite only having direct  control over noctus which makes for a  satisfying juggling act once you  understand the game's demanding pace in  the extent of your abilities though you  can pause the action to re-equip  characters and use items mid-battle  combat is otherwise a non-stop fluid  process by holding down a button noctus  will deliver a combo attack until he's  interrupted by an enemy if you're quick  you can press another button to phase  through an incoming attack and continue  your assault  noctus can also warp attack from great  distances swap between four weapons made  combo if need be cast magic and our rare  occasions summon godlike Astral's onto  the battlefield to mop up enemies  Astral's are powerful beings that align  with Noctis throughout the story to be  summoned later in a time of need but  each of the four Astral's you acquire  calls for very specific battle and  weather conditions meaning you have very  little control over when they actually  appear where you could always count on  summons to save the day in previous  Final Fantasy games it's disheartening  that they usually fail to appear during  Final Fantasy 15 s most difficult  battles more often than not you can at  least rely on magic to hammer tough  enemies when Astral's seem out of reach  spells can be crafted by bottling ice  fire and lightning harvested from  elemental springs and dungeons in the  overworld and you can also combine these  elements with items for increased  potency and extra status effects it's  important to pay attention what you cast  but also where you cast it as your party  can suffer frostbite burns and shock if  they are standing too close to the point  of impact while this may sound bad it  has an appreciable layer of strategy to  combat that makes you weigh the risks  and benefits of taking the easy way out  as you earn experience and level up your  party earns ability points that can be  spent to upgrade things like AI  behaviors in battle or bolster noctis's  suite of skills you can also unlock  passive abilities that help you earn  money and experience points faster as  you explore the open world but all told  EP is in short supply and the Ascension  grid is fractured into many categories  making it difficult to decide where to  focus your efforts ultimately  accessories do the heavy lifting when it  comes to character customization they  typically increase characters stats but  also offer protection from status  ailments and influence your companions  behaviors most weapons are less exciting  and varied and you may be shocked and  disappointed when you discover that each  merchant only carries one or two for the  entirety of the game and don't be fooled  by the outfits menu no one sells outfits  in the game meaning you're stuck with  your initial set which is 2 per  character or 4 if you count optional  jackets it seems odd that there are so  few options not only because a menu  screen is dedicated to them but because  the few outfits you can wear come with  small but noticeable effects on your  party's attributes presuming you let it  pull you along with minimal side  tracking it's possible to finish Final  Fantasy 15 story in just over 30 hours  this is short by Final Fantasy standards  but after the credits roll the real fun  is just getting started over 60 hours  into my quest  I recently discovered strange locked  doors unlike anything else I've seen up  until this point nested inside the inner  sanctums of already high level dungeons  I have no idea how to open them but my  party's amazement in addition to my own  is enough to make me want to find a way  I'm also in the middle of a quest line  that promises to reward me with the most  powerful weapons in the land but only if  I can take down massive creatures that  rival even the Astral's impressive scale  Final Fantasy 15s in-game content is  some of the best in the entire game and  when it's all said and done these are  the moments I will remember most it's  been a long ten years since Final  Fantasy 15 was first revealed and  tasting games have changed in the  meantime  while it's safe to assume fans and  Outsiders will find some aspect of Final  Fantasy 15 disappointing be at the  shallow story or the outlandish cast it  would be hard for anyone to deny that  Final Fantasy 15 is a fascinating  experience whereas characters fail to  impress Final Fantasy 15 beautiful world  and exciting challenges save the day  [Music]
 

